# Feature branches from plan titles

When starting a **new feature** in this repo (new OpenSpec/Linear change, new implementation plan, or first implementation work for a planned feature):

1. Create and check out a branch **before** editing product code.
2. Name it from the **plan title** (or the OpenSpec change / Linear issue title you are building), not a vague label like `feature` or `wip`.
3. Use the `cursor/` prefix, then a git-safe slug of that title: lowercase, spaces and punctuation → hyphens, collapse repeats, trim edges. Keep it readable and under ~60 characters when possible.
4. If the title or plan mentions a Linear id (`MSHO-13`, etc.), keep that id in the slug so PRs stay linked (e.g. plan `F9 Command Registry MVP (Linear MSHO-13)` → `cursor/f9-command-registry-mvp-linear-msho-13`).
5. Do not reuse `master` / `main` for feature work. Do not rename an unrelated existing branch to match a new plan.

## Examples

| Plan title | Branch |
| --- | --- |
| F9 Command Registry MVP (Linear MSHO-13) | `cursor/f9-command-registry-mvp-linear-msho-13` |
| Soften crop handles | `cursor/soften-crop-handles` |

## Out of scope

Routine fixes on an already-correct feature branch, or chores that are not tied to a named plan, do not require a new branch from a plan title.
